<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Harold Godwinson</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1022–1066</span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Harold II of England, Harold II</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Harold Godwinson was the last crowned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anglo-saxons">Anglo-Saxon</a> King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, reigning as Harold II from January to October 1066. Son of Earl Godwin of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wessex">Wessex</a>, he was the realm's leading noble under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edward-the-confessor">Edward the Confessor</a> and campaigned in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a> in 1063. After defeating a Norwegian invasion at Stamford Bridge, he was killed at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-hastings">Battle of Hastings</a> by the army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-the-conqueror">William of Normandy</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/harold-godwinson.jpg" alt="Harold Godwinson" width="320" height="270" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: ~ · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bayeux_tapestry_stitches_detail..jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
